@startuml c4-dynamic
!include ../vendor/style.puml

title Dynamic view — durable acceptance, chain confirmation and proof export

autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #438DD5
  FontColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E6DA4
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  GroupBorderColor #999999
  GroupHeaderFontColor #444444
}
participant "Portal / ERP" as client
participant "Traceability App" as app
participant "Operational PostgreSQL" as db
participant "Batch Builder / Relayer" as relayer
participant "Public Blockchain" as chain #999999
participant "Projection Workers" as workers
participant "Public CDN" as cdn

== Phase 1 · Validate and durably accept ==
client -> client: Retain signed submission locally
client -> app: Signed EPCIS event, captureRecordId and profile reference
app -> app: Validate profile, active membership and current key
app -> db: Atomic commit: signed event, acceptance receipt,\nadmission evidence and anchor intent
app --> client: Acceptance receipt: PENDING_ANCHOR
note over app, db: Return a receipt only after transaction commit.\nA receipt is not chain confirmation or a zero-loss recovery promise.\nRevoked keys are rejected; duplicate submissions are idempotent.

== Phase 2 · Batch and anchor ==
relayer -> db: Claim anchor intents; persist deterministic leaves\nand ordered batch manifest
relayer -> chain: Submit sequenced root linked to previous root
chain --> relayer: Observe consensus finality; transaction reference
relayer -> db: Persist finality and inclusion proofs
note over relayer, chain: Chain outages leave accepted events pending and retry.\nNo timeout promotes an event to CONFIRMED.

== Phase 3 · Confirm and project ==
workers -> db: Check durable event and finalised leaf; mark CONFIRMED
workers -> cdn: Publish versioned public projection

== Phase 4 · Export verification material ==
client -> app: Request scoped confirmation proof bundle
app -> db: Read event, signature, receipt, key/version evidence,\nbatch manifest, inclusion proof and chain reference
app --> client: Confirmation proof bundle
client -> client: Retain bundle; independently check public-chain commitment
note over client, db: Database PITR and encrypted backups support ordinary service recovery.\nBackup completion is not on the acceptance path; roots cannot restore missing payloads.
@enduml
